+# The Daily Grind
+
+A static homepage with a client-side coffee finder. No build step or dependencies are required.
+
+## Coffee finder
+
+The homepage form exposes the declarative WebMCP tool `find_coffee` using `toolname`, `tooldescription`, and `toolautosubmit`. Named, labeled selects provide its parameters:
+
+- `temperature`: `any`, `hot`, or `iced`
+- `flavor`: `any`, `bold`, `smooth`, or `sweet`
+- `milk`: `any`, `oat`, or `none`
+
+Example input: `{"temperature":"iced","flavor":"smooth","milk":"none"}` recommends Cold Brew.
+
+Human and agent submissions run the same handler in `coffee-finder.js`. Agent submissions receive a structured result through `SubmitEvent.respondWith()`, including the recommendation, submitted preferences, whether the match is exact, and matched and unmatched preferences. Milk preference takes priority, then temperature, then flavor; ties follow menu order. This finder recommends existing menu items and does not place orders.
+
+Native tool discovery requires a browser and agent supporting the [WebMCP declarative API](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/webmcp/declarative-api). The form also works as an ordinary JavaScript form without WebMCP support. API-specific event handling is feature-checked.
+
+Static checks: `node --check coffee-finder.js` and `git diff --check`. There is no build script.
