+# smallpt studio
+
+Kevin Beason's smallpt C++ path tracer, compiled to WebAssembly with Emscripten. Open `index.html` through a static HTTP host. No application server or backend is needed. The renderer runs in a module web worker and progressively draws RGBA frames to a canvas. Sphere colors, sample count, resolution, reset, and PNG export are supported.
+
+The original source is preserved in `vendor/smallpt.cpp`, under the MIT license in `vendor/LICENSE.txt`. `src/renderer.cpp` adapts its rendering loop to progressive batches and exposes scene colors and pixel memory. `public/preview.png` is a native render of the same scene, shown while WebAssembly initializes.
+
+## Rebuild
+
+Install Emscripten and make `emcc` available, then run:
+
+```sh
+npm run build
+```
+
+This regenerates `public/smallpt.js` and `public/smallpt.wasm`. Both compiled files are included, so rebuilding is optional. No cross-origin isolation headers are required. Use a current browser with WebAssembly and module worker support.
+
+Higher sample counts reduce Monte Carlo noise at the cost of CPU time. A new render cancels the previous render between row batches.
+
+Original project: https://www.kevinbeason.com/smallpt/
