+# smallpt — a browser path-tracing playground

-This project is a sample news application built with Astro, designed to serve as a testing ground for new features in Chrome DevTools.
+Kevin Beason’s [smallpt](https://www.kevinbeason.com/smallpt/) C++ path tracer compiled to WebAssembly with Emscripten. The home page is prerendered to `dist/client/index.html`. Rendering runs locally in a module Web Worker; no server computation, uploads, or cross-origin isolation are required.

+The interface starts a render automatically. Randomize & render changes the mirror and glass sphere colors and the sphere-based side walls. Sample and resolution controls rerender the current palette; reset restores the original Cornell box. The gallery loads reproducible seeded scenes. Completed renders can be downloaded as PNGs.
+
+## Build
+
+Install Node.js 22+ and Emscripten (`em++` on PATH), then run:

 ```sh
-pnpm install && pnpm run start
+pnpm install
+pnpm build
+pnpm check:wasm
 ```

-The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
+The build compiles `native/renderer.cpp` into `public/wasm/smallpt.js` and `smallpt.wasm` before building Astro. The checked-in Wasm artifacts are also ready to use. The site’s existing Astro server routes remain available, while the playground itself is static.
+
+`pnpm check:wasm` executes the exact browser binary in Node without a browser or server. It checks meaningful image output, deterministic seeds, color randomization of both object spheres, progressive batch equivalence, and original scene reset.
+
+`pnpm build:studies` optionally regenerates the two gallery previews using the same WebAssembly renderer at 640 × 480, 128 samples per pixel. These are real rendered images. The initial preview is the original smallpt distribution’s `result_25k.png`.
+
+## Source and license

-## Tech Stack
+- `vendor/smallpt/smallpt.cpp`: upstream source; the only change wraps its CLI `main` with `SMALLPT_LIBRARY` so the browser adapter can reuse the renderer.
+- `native/renderer.cpp`: framebuffer, seeded palettes, and progressive row adapter; retains the original radiance, materials, and camera calculations.
+- `public/wasm/render-worker.js`: loads Wasm and transfers progressive RGBA frames to the UI.
+- `src/pages/index.astro`: playground, rendered to `index.html` by the build.

-- **[Astro](https://astro.build/)**: The web framework for building content-driven websites.
-- **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
-- **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
-- **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
