+The static page loads `coffee-card.js`, which registers the autonomous
+`<coffee-card>` custom element. Each instance owns its shadow DOM and styles;
+the site's `--primary` CSS variable can customize its accent color.
+
+| Attribute / property | Type | Default | Behavior |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `name` | string | `''` | Card heading |
+| `description` | string | `''` | Card description |
+| `href` | string | `''` | Details destination; omitted when empty |
+| `price` | number or `null` | `null` | Optional USD price with two decimal places |
+| `disabled` | boolean | `false` | Disables the details link |
+
+Properties reflect to attributes; attribute changes immediately update properties
+and rendering. Assigning `null` to a string property or `price` removes its
+attribute. The `price` setter accepts finite, non-negative numbers and throws a
+`TypeError` otherwise. Invalid or empty price attributes hide the price.
+Boolean attributes follow HTML presence semantics: `disabled="false"` still
+disables the link; set `card.disabled = false` or remove the attribute to enable it.
+
+```html
+<coffee-card name="Oat Latte" description="Smooth and creamy."
+  href="/menu/latte" price="4.50"></coffee-card>
+```
