@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+# The Daily Grind
+
+Static homepage with browser-only signing and verification of coffee receipts and gift vouchers. Serve the files over HTTPS (localhost also permits Web Crypto). No build step or external crypto dependency is required.
+
+The workspace prefers native ML-DSA-65 when the browser advertises support and its key generation/export/sign/verify path succeeds. Otherwise it tries Ed25519, then ECDSA P-256 with SHA-256. The selected algorithm is shown next to the key fingerprint. Verification uses the document's specified algorithm and never substitutes a different algorithm.
+
+Non-exportable private CryptoKeys are saved in IndexedDB. If storage is unavailable, a session-only key is generated with a visible notice. Public keys can be exported as JSON. Clearing browser storage removes the local signing identity; keep exported public keys to verify older documents. No private-key export is offered.
+
+Signed JSON includes the format version, algorithm, and complete document. Keys are canonically ordered before signing. ML-DSA uses a fixed application context; classical algorithms sign a length-prefixed context followed by the canonical document. Verifiers reject unsupported formats and require a separate public key, using the browser's own local public key by default or an explicitly supplied trusted issuer key.
+
+This static workspace demonstrates local issuer authenticity and document integrity. It cannot establish Daily Grind merchant identity, confirm payment, or enforce voucher redemption, expiration, revocation, or single use. Production merchant issuance requires a merchant-controlled private key and an independently authenticated public-key distribution channel. Do not distribute a merchant private key to customer browsers.
+
+Run `npm test` for automated Web Crypto checks for valid receipts/vouchers, tampering, wrong keys, domain separation, public-key fingerprints, malformed inputs, key non-exportability, and the classical fallback algorithms. Node 24+ supports the native ML-DSA path; Node may report experimental API warnings. No browser or development server is needed to run these tests.
