@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+# The Daily Grind
+
+A static coffee homepage with browser-based ECDSA P-256 / SHA-256 signatures for demo receipts and gift vouchers. No payment is collected; vouchers have no redeemable value.
+
+Serve the files from an HTTPS origin (or localhost). Web Crypto and IndexedDB must be available. There are no runtime JavaScript dependencies and no build step.
+
+## Documents and trust
+
+The first visit generates a non-exportable private key and stores the CryptoKey pair in IndexedDB. Subsequent visits on the same origin and browser profile reuse it. A SHA-256 public-key fingerprint identifies the locally trusted signer. Private keys are never included in downloads.
+
+A signed JSON envelope contains a versioned payload, algorithm, key fingerprint, and signature. Canonical serialization sorts object keys, preserves array order, and signs all envelope metadata along with the payload. Verification enforces the supported schema and checks against the saved local public key; it never trusts a key supplied by an uploaded document. Amounts use integer cents.
+
+Downloads are portable files, but **trust is local to the issuing browser**. A different browser or cleared site storage cannot authenticate older documents. Signatures establish local key origin and unchanged contents. They do not establish merchant identity, payment, voucher redemption state, or prevent copying a valid voucher. Same-origin scripts have access to use the signing key, so this is not an authorization boundary against compromised application code.
+
+For real merchant issuance, provision an authenticated merchant trust anchor and an authorized signing service or separately controlled issuer device. Payment and one-time redemption need authenticated backend records. Do not ship a merchant private key in client code or automatically trust uploaded public keys.
+
+## Automated checks
+
+- `npm run check` — JavaScript syntax checks.
+- `npm test` — real Web Crypto round trips, private-key non-exportability, tampering, unknown signers, malformed input, and canonicalization.
+
+Photography is loaded from Unsplash; typefaces are loaded from Google Fonts with system fallbacks. No browser automation or preview server is needed for these checks.
