@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+Client-side paint monitoring loads from `performance-monitor.js` without changing links or adding a router.
+
+`window.dailyGrindPerformance.supported` identifies browser support for interaction contentful paints and soft navigations. Unsupported APIs are skipped; there is no timer approximation masquerading as actual paint completion.
+
+Use `window.dailyGrindPerformance.getReports()` to read the latest 200 reports, or subscribe to `window.addEventListener('daily-grind:performance', ({ detail }) => { /* analytics integration */ })`. No analytics endpoint is configured and no data is sent over the network. `disconnect()` flushes the active route and removes monitoring listeners and observers.
+
+Interaction reports include an action label (`navigation:*`, `order-now`, or `seasonal:*`), interaction ID, start timestamp, paint/presentation timestamps, duration in milliseconds, and painted content size. Each progressively larger contentful paint produces a candidate report, including asynchronous updates caused by the input. A candidate measures interaction-to-presentation latency; it is not a promise that all pixels or animations have finished. Inputs producing no contentful paint produce no report. Pointer and keyboard input timestamps attribute paints to the annotated control, including descendants of seasonal cards.
+
+Soft-navigation reports include the destination URL, navigation and interaction IDs, FCP duration, and the latest largest contentful paint duration/size. They finalize at the next soft navigation, when the document becomes hidden, or on pagehide. Early paints are seeded from `getLargestInteractionContentfulPaint()`; later paints are correlated by interaction ID rather than navigation ID. View switches without a URL change can produce interaction paint reports but are not browser soft navigations. Buffered entries from before input listeners were installed can lack an action label.
+
+The current links perform full document navigations. This page cannot measure a destination document's paint; that requires monitoring on the destination. Monitoring does not intercept navigation or invent client-side views. These experimental paint entry types are feature-detected and unavailable in some browsers. Existing initial-load metrics, if added separately, can continue unchanged.
+
+Run the isolated observer and lifecycle checks with `node --test tests/performance-monitor.test.cjs`. These use simulated performance entries and do not start a server or browser.
