+++ b/PERFORMANCE.md
@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@
+Homepage performance monitoring loads automatically from `performance-monitor.js`.
+It measures navigation links, Order Now, and clicks anywhere in a Seasonal
+Favorites card (including keyboard-generated link clicks). Link behavior is unchanged.
+
+Read the latest 100 records with `window.dailyGrindPerformance.getSamples()`,
+inspect `daily-grind:*` User Timing measures, or subscribe for collection:
+
+```js
+window.addEventListener('daily-grind:performance', ({ detail }) => {
+  console.log(detail.type, detail.target, detail.duration, detail.source);
+});
+```
+
+Durations are milliseconds. `event-timing` uses the browser's click-to-next-paint
+duration, including input delay, handler processing, and presentation delay. The
+browser rounds these durations and only exposes events above its reporting
+threshold (requested at 16 ms). Other clicks use `after-paint-estimate`: a timer
+scheduled inside requestAnimationFrame. Its duration includes task scheduling
+delay and is an approximation of the next rendering opportunity. Reporting may
+wait another 100 ms for Event Timing; that wait is excluded from the duration.
+These are individual click measurements, not the page's aggregate INP score.
+
+History pushState/replaceState and popstate/hashchange automatically measure
+synchronous client-side view updates through the following rendering opportunity.
+The current homepage has no router. For asynchronous views or views that do not
+change the URL, explicitly bracket the update:
+
+```js
+const painted = window.dailyGrindPerformance.startViewSwitch('menu');
+await loadMenu();
+renderMenu();
+painted(); // Call after the DOM commit, including any framework render scheduling.
+```
+
+Explicit view timing includes asynchronous work before the completion callback;
+automatic History API timing cannot infer when later asynchronous work commits.
+Both use `after-paint-estimate`. An explicit measurement and a History API call
+produce separate records. Timings end at the next paint opportunity, not at the
+end of CSS transitions or subsequent image loads. Full document navigation is
+outside this document's scope: the original links still navigate normally, and
+unloading/hidden pages discard unfinished measurements. Uncompleted explicit
+measurements expire after 30 seconds. No analytics requests or user data are sent.
+
+Run automated checks with `node --test performance-monitor.test.cjs`.
