@@ -2,6 +2,33 @@

 This project is a sample news application built with Astro, designed to serve as a testing ground for new features in Chrome DevTools.

+## Developer diagnostics
+
+The homepage includes independent browser-side connection checks for a private LAN
+hardware device and a loopback companion CLI. Defaults are examples:
+`http://192.168.1.100:8080/health` and `http://127.0.0.1:8787/health`.
+Replace these with your services' actual read-only health endpoints. A successful
+2xx response reports reachability and latency; the widget does not open a persistent
+session, execute CLI commands, or collect response payloads.
+
+Serve the site over HTTPS (localhost is also a secure context). Connect initiates
+a credential-free CORS GET directly from the reader's browser, with
+`targetAddressSpace: 'local'` for hardware and `'loopback'` for the CLI. Nothing is
+proxied by the news server. The endpoint must return
+`Access-Control-Allow-Origin` allowing the site's origin, even on error responses;
+browser permission does not replace CORS. Use a dedicated read-only endpoint and
+configure the companion service to listen on loopback. Requests reject redirects.
+
+Browsers supporting granular Local Network Access permissions may prompt
+separately for `local-network` and `loopback-network`. Denials can be changed in
+the browser's site settings. Unsupported permission queries fall back to a
+user-initiated connection attempt; browsers without the relevant local HTTP
+support may still block it. Checks time out after 15 seconds and can be canceled.
+No device discovery, background polling, or automatic connection runs on load.
+
+See [Chrome's Local Network Access guidance](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/modern-web-guidance/guides/security/local-network-access)
+for browser behavior and endpoint requirements.
+

 ```sh
 pnpm install && pnpm run start
