 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Account settings and passkeys
+
+Account settings are at `/devtools-times/account/settings`. Password sign-in still
+uses the existing Times login service; successful authentication now creates an
+HttpOnly, SameSite session. Readers can register discoverable passkeys, sign in
+with them, rename their account labels, and revoke them. Removing the final key
+is allowed because password sign-in remains available.
+
+Passkey data and hashed session tokens persist in SQLite using Node's built-in
+`node:sqlite` module (Node 22.13+). Set `ACCOUNT_DATABASE_PATH` to a database file
+on a persistent, access-controlled volume; it defaults to `.data/accounts.sqlite`.
+The included storage is intended for a single Node deployment. Multiple replicas
+need a shared transactional database implementation rather than separate local
+SQLite files. Back up the database to preserve reader IDs and credential records.
+Existing passkeys held by another authentication service must be migrated with
+their original user handles, RP IDs, public keys, counters, and timestamps; the
+app does not invent or seed credentials.
+
+Set `PASSKEY_ORIGIN` to the exact public HTTPS origin (without a path) and
+`PASSKEY_RP_ID` to the registration domain in production, especially behind a
+reverse proxy. Defaults come from the server request URL. Keep both settings
+stable after registration. All registration and authentication challenges are
+single-use, expire after five minutes, and require authenticator user verification.
+Credential mutations check both the signed-in reader and request origin.
+
+The browser Signal API receives the complete accepted credential list on settings
+load and after removal. Unsupported browsers retain full account management and
+show manual password-manager cleanup instructions. Renaming an individual key
+only updates its account label; it does not rename the user's authenticator
+profile. Provider metadata is a local snapshot from
+[passkey-authenticator-aaguids](https://github.com/passkeydeveloper/passkey-authenticator-aaguids),
+used only for display. The snapshot retains names and light icons up to 3 KB,
+omitting dark and larger icon payloads. Unknown and zero AAGUIDs, or providers
+without a compact icon, receive a generic key icon.
