@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+# The Daily Grind
+
+A responsive, static café homepage and account workspace. Open `index.html` through an existing HTTPS or localhost static hosting environment. No build is required.
+
+## Account flows
+
+The initial account is an explicitly labeled sample with example devices. Sample profile and passkey changes remain in memory. Choose **Create an account** to register a real browser-local account with WebAuthn, then sign out and sign in using its email and passkey in the same browser.
+
+- Registration creates a discoverable ES256 passkey with required user verification.
+- Sign-in validates the challenge, origin, RP ID hash, user-presence and user-verification flags, user handle, signature, and signature counter.
+- Profile updates and adding, renaming, or removing passkeys require a fresh assertion from an existing passkey.
+- The last real passkey cannot be removed. Removing a credential from this account does not delete it from its passkey provider.
+- Canceled requests and unsupported browsers show an inline explanation.
+
+## Scope
+
+This repository has no backend. Profiles and public credentials are stored in localStorage, and the current local session is stored in sessionStorage. This is an interactive browser-local demonstration, not a production security boundary. Browser storage can be modified by the user; clearing it loses these local accounts. A synced passkey alone does not transfer the local account to another browser.
+
+For production, move challenge generation, credential and account storage, assertion validation, replay prevention, session issuance, and authorization to a trusted server. Add account recovery and email ownership verification before treating an email address as verified.
+
+Menu, order, rewards, and café information are preview content. Stock photography comes from Unsplash; fonts load from Google Fonts.
+
+## Checks
+
+`node --check app.js` checks JavaScript syntax. No dev or preview server is required for this check.
