@@ -15,3 +15,42 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Passkeys and account settings
+
+Sign in and sign up at `/devtools-times/signin` and `/devtools-times/signup`.
+After password sign-in or account creation, readers can register a passkey.
+Sign-in also supports discoverable passkeys through its button and username autofill.
+`/devtools-times/account/settings` lists passkeys, allows creation, renaming and
+removal, and supports display-name updates and sign-out. Sensitive changes require
+a password or an existing account-bound passkey when the last identity check is
+more than five minutes old. Password authentication still uses the existing
+remote Times API; passwords and biometric information are never stored locally.
+
+The same-origin `/devtools-times/api/auth/*` API uses SimpleWebAuthn for server-side
+verification, single-use session-bound challenges, required user verification,
+credential ownership checks and signature counters. Native browser WebAuthn calls
+use `webauthn-polyfills` for JSON conversion and capability detection. Optional
+Signal API calls synchronize accepted credentials and account details without
+blocking account actions on unsupported browsers.
+
+Runtime requirements:
+
+- Use Node.js 24 or newer (the credential store uses `node:sqlite`).
+- Set `WEBAUTHN_ORIGIN` to the exact public HTTPS origin (no path), for example
+  `https://news.example.com`. It defaults to the configured Astro site origin;
+  localhost requests use their local origin for development.
+- Optionally set `WEBAUTHN_RP_ID` to the configured relying-party domain. It
+  defaults to the hostname of `WEBAUTHN_ORIGIN`. Keep this value stable: changing
+  it makes existing passkeys unusable. It must be valid for the configured origin.
+- Set `AUTH_DB_PATH` to a persistent SQLite file. The default is
+  `./data/auth.sqlite`, ignored by Git. Back up this file and use a single
+  application instance with persistent disk. Ephemeral or independently scaled
+  containers need a shared database implementation before deployment.
+
+Passkey provider names and small provider icons are a local snapshot of the
+[passkey authenticator AAGUID registry](https://github.com/passkeydeveloper/passkey-authenticator-aaguids).
+Repeated icons are deduplicated; large or absent icons use a generic key symbol.
+Provider metadata is used only for display, never for security decisions. Unknown
+and zero AAGUIDs use a neutral fallback. Account usernames remain managed by the
+remote password service; only the local display name is editable here.
