 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Accounts and passkeys
+
+The sign-in, sign-up, and `/devtools-times/account/settings` pages support discoverable passkeys, password sign-in, and passkey management. WebAuthn ceremonies use SimpleWebAuthn with required user verification, expiring single-use challenges, origin/RP verification, and server-side public-key storage. Management requires verification within the last five minutes; the UI offers passkey or password reauthentication when needed. A passwordless account cannot remove its last passkey.
+
+Run on **Node 22.13 or newer**. Account data uses SQLite at `.data/auth.sqlite`. Set `AUTH_DB_PATH` to a private persistent volume in deployment; instances must share the same authoritative database (this file-backed implementation is intended for a single server). Set `AUTH_ORIGIN` to the canonical public origin, e.g. `https://example.com`, behind a reverse proxy. Use HTTPS in production; localhost also supports WebAuthn. Passkeys are bound to the origin's hostname, so keep that hostname stable.
+
+Existing password accounts are verified against the original Times login API and linked to the local account store on their first successful sign-in. Their password authentication and password reauthentication continue to use that API, while their passkeys are managed locally. Newly registered accounts use the local store. No private passkey material, biometric data, or raw session tokens are stored by the application.
+
+Validation: `pnpm run build` and `pnpm run test:auth`. Browser/device passkey prompts require a supported authenticator. Password sign-in remains available for accounts created with a password.
