+# Privacy design and deployment
+
+This repository is a static brochure site. It has no backend, client JavaScript,
+forms, cookies, browser storage, analytics, advertising, or runtime dependencies.
+Do not add data collection without reviewing necessity, purpose, retention,
+access control, deletion, and the public privacy notice first. Do not place
+personal data or secrets in HTML, URLs, logs, or browser storage.
+
+## Third-party audit
+
+- The original Unsplash CSS background sent visitors' IP addresses and request
+  metadata to images.unsplash.com. The same photo is now served locally as
+  assets/coffee.jpg. Original source:
+  https://unsplash.com/photos/4d71bcdd2085 and
+  https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1495474472287-4d71bcdd2085
+- Fonts use the device's system fonts; there are no third-party font requests.
+- No third-party scripts, embeds, tracking pixels, or runtime packages exist.
+- The existing start command uses pnpm dlx statikk, which downloads a development
+  tool. It is not a production security-header configuration. The build and
+  privacy audit use Node built-ins and require no package downloads.
+- Hosting remains a data processor: before launch, review the chosen provider's
+  access logs, retention, access controls, geographic processing, and contracts.
+  No provider or log retention policy is configured in this repository.
+
+Run `npm run audit:privacy` and `npm test` before accepting new resources or
+vendors. The audit is a static regression guard, not a full security scanner or
+an independent third-party certification. Review new packages and resource types
+manually in code review. External integrations require a new vendor assessment.
+
+## Deployment
+
+Run `npm run build` and publish only `dist/`. Netlify uses netlify.toml and the
+published _headers file; Vercel uses vercel.json. Other hosts must apply the same
+headers at their HTTPS edge. Header files are configuration, not proof that an
+arbitrary host serves those headers. Do not publish the repository root.
+
+The HTML CSP and referrer meta tags provide fallback protection. Framing
+protection, Permissions-Policy, nosniff, HSTS, and the other response headers
+require host support. CSP disables all scripts, network APIs, forms, frames,
+workers, and plugins; only local styles and images are allowed. No CSP report
+endpoint is configured because reports can contain browsing information.
+
+Enforce HTTPS redirects at the host. HSTS lasts one year without applying to
+subdomains or requesting preload. Check actual response headers on the deployed
+host before release. See the [CSP specification](https://www.w3.org/TR/CSP/)
+for the distinction between response headers and meta policies.
+
+## Secure data handling for future services
+
+Existing account, rewards, and ordering links have no implementation here.
+The misleading GET logout link was removed; a real logout must use an
+authenticated POST with CSRF protection, invalidate the server session, and clear
+its cookie. Authentication must use server-managed Secure, HttpOnly, SameSite
+cookies; never place session tokens or payment details in client storage. Keep
+private responses uncached and validate/authorize all operations server-side.
+Use a reviewed payment provider rather than handling card details in this site.
+Define actual retention/deletion rules and update the notice before enabling
+such services. These server controls cannot be implemented in this static site.
