new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a85d4ae
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/privacy-audit.md
@@ -0,0 +1,35 @@
+# Privacy audit
+
+Scope: sign-in/sign-up forms, shared page layout, document headers, and the privacy notice.
+
+| Finding | Change |
+| --- | --- |
+| Analytics ran automatically, including on credential pages. | Removed the analytics script and the commented ad loader. No optional analytics or advertising script loads. |
+| Google Fonts connections occurred on each page load. | Removed remote font stylesheets and preconnects; existing serif fallback supplies the brand font. |
+| Account fields had no explanation of their purpose or recipient. | Both forms identify the Google Cloud account service and link the privacy notice. Sign-up encourages a pseudonymous username. No additional account fields were introduced. |
+| Backend errors were displayed verbatim. | Both forms use generic failures; response bodies and returned tokens are not read or stored. |
+| Requests relied on browser defaults. | Shared POST helper sends only username/password, explicitly omits cookies, suppresses referrers, disables caching, and rejects redirects to avoid forwarding credentials. |
+| Passwords remained in component state after a request. | Clear passwords in the completion path for success, HTTP failures, and network failures. Keep password-manager autocomplete support. |
+| Document headers lacked a referrer policy. | Add no-referrer HTML metadata and an HTTP Referrer-Policy header in shared middleware. Account pages also return private, no-store caching headers. |
+| Middleware initialized a reading-list session for every visitor. | Let the existing reading-list POST endpoint initialize storage only when an article is saved. GET already defaults to an empty list. |
+| The privacy policy was generic and made unsupported claims. | Describe actual account handling, reading-list sessions, external images, and unknown backend retention details. |
+
+Forms remain disabled until their submit handler is mounted, and use POST as a fallback to keep credentials out of URLs. Existing sign-up password guidance is now enforced with HTML validation. No new analytics consent UI is necessary while optional scripts remain absent.
+
+## Limits
+
+The external account service is outside this repository. Its password storage, logs, retention periods, and deletion process have not been audited. The existing form only reports authentication success and has no persistent authenticated session. External article images still contact their providers. Some demonstration articles contain their own scripts; those are outside this layout/form audit. Removing the remote font uses the existing local serif fallback, so typography may differ.
+
+## Validation
+
+- `node --test tests/auth.test.mjs`: four mocked tests cover both request payloads/options, non-JSON success responses, safe HTTP failure handling, and network failures. No real credentials or requests are used.
+- `pnpm run build`: production compilation only.
+- `git diff --check`: whitespace check.
+
+No browser verification, server startup, or server entrypoint import was performed.
+
+## References
+
+- [Astro middleware](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/middleware/) supports response changes in shared request middleware.
+- [MDN Referrer-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Headers/Referrer-Policy) documents no-referrer behavior.
+- [Fetch standard](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/) defines request credential, cache, redirect, and referrer handling.
