--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,3 +15,20 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## SMS sign-up verification
+
+Copy `.env.example` to `.env` for local builds, or configure the three server environment variables in your deployment: `TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID`, `TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN`, and `TWILIO_FROM_NUMBER` (an SMS-capable Twilio sender). Credentials stay on the server. Delivery uses the [Twilio Messages API](https://www.twilio.com/docs/messaging/api/message-resource); missing configuration fails closed instead of simulating verification.
+
+Sign-up collects an international phone number and sends a six-digit code. The server stores an HMAC of the code in the Astro session, enforces a five-minute expiry and five incorrect attempts, and consumes the code before calling the existing registration service. Resending replaces the previous code and is limited to once per minute per session. A failed registration requires a new code. Preserve the session cookie between steps; for multiple server instances, configure Astro's session storage with a shared backing store. Apply deployment-level SMS rate limits and Twilio spending/geographic restrictions, since a per-session cooldown alone does not prevent abuse across new sessions.
+
+SMS messages finish with `@hostname #code`, using the request's hostname without its scheme, port, or path. Serve the sign-up page over HTTPS at the same hostname used for its API requests. WebOTP is feature-detected, with keyboard one-time-code autofill and manual entry as fallbacks. The listener starts before sending each SMS and is aborted on submit, resend, navigation, and unmount.
+
+The local registration endpoint gates this application's flow and forwards `phoneNumber` alongside the existing username and password. The separately hosted registration service must also enforce verification if it accepts registration from other clients; its source and phone storage contract are outside this repository.
+
+Validation without starting a server:
+
+```sh
+node --test tests/signup.test.ts
+pnpm build
+```
