+
+## Phone verification for sign-up
+
+The sign-up form sends SMS codes through Twilio Verify. The local `api/signup`
+endpoint checks the code with Twilio before calling the existing registration API.
+No provider credentials or verification decisions are sent to the browser.
+
+Set these **server runtime** environment variables (for local builds, export them
+in your shell; the Node deployment must also receive them at runtime):
+
+```sh
+TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=AC...
+TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=...
+TWILIO_VERIFY_SERVICE_SID=VA...
+```
+
+Create a Verify service with six-digit codes and SMS enabled. Enable Twilio Fraud
+Guard and configure service rate limits/allowed destination countries for your
+traffic. The endpoint also applies a per-phone resend delay within each server
+process; use shared gateway limits for deployments with multiple instances.
+Missing configuration returns a service-unavailable error; codes are never mocked.
+
+Automatic extraction uses WebOTP on supported browsers over HTTPS, with
+`autocomplete="one-time-code"` and manual typing/pasting as fallbacks. Configure a
+[Twilio custom verification template](https://www.twilio.com/docs/verify/verification-templates)
+whose final line contains the exact deployment hostname and code, for example:
+
+```text
+123456 is your DevTools Times verification code.
+@example.com #123456
+```
+
+Replace the code with the provider's template variable and the hostname with the
+host serving the sign-up page (without scheme or path). WebOTP listens before
+requesting SMS delivery, fills the input with user consent, and leaves submission
+under the user's control. See the [WebOTP documentation](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/WebOTP_API).
+
+A code is consumed when Twilio approves it. If the external registration service
+then fails, request a fresh code before retrying. The external registration
+service must also enforce phone verification for any clients that call it directly;
+this repository can enforce it only through its own sign-up endpoint.
+
+Run verification tests with `node --test tests/*.test.ts` (Node 24 or newer).
