+# Daily Grind
+
+Responsive coffee homepage with Google-verified rewards registration. No OTP or magic-link emails are sent.
+
+## Configure
+
+Requires Node 22.13+ (Node 24 recommended) and pnpm.
+
+1. Install dependencies with `pnpm install`.
+2. Copy `.env.example` to `.env`.
+3. Create a Google Cloud OAuth client of type **Web application**. Add the site's exact origin to **Authorized JavaScript origins** and set `GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID` in `.env`.
+4. Set `APP_ORIGIN` to the public site origin, including scheme and port if applicable. Use HTTPS in production. Set `PORT` to the hosting port.
+5. `pnpm start` serves both the page and the API. Static-only hosting cannot run account registration.
+
+The interface remains usable without configuration but verification reports unavailability; it never simulates verification. Customers must use Gmail or Google Workspace addresses: Google is not authoritative for arbitrary third-party account emails. See [Google's server verification guidance](https://developers.google.com/identity/gsi/web/guides/verify-google-id-token).
+
+## Flow
+
+- `GET /api/auth/config`: public client ID and a random nonce; sets a ten-minute HttpOnly, SameSite signup cookie.
+- `POST /api/verify-email`: `{credential, email}`. The Google library verifies the signed ID token and audience; the endpoint also checks issuer, expiry, email verification, authoritative email provider, nonce, and entered-email match. No email address alone can establish ownership.
+- `POST /api/rewards/signup`: `{firstName, lastName, email, marketing}`. Requires server-held verification, stores an account, consumes the signup session, and sets a random HttpOnly account session cookie. Only its hash is stored.
+
+Accounts and sessions persist in `data/rewards.sqlite` (override with `DATABASE_PATH`). Keep the database private and back it up. Pending verification and rate limits are in process memory; use shared storage for a multi-instance deployment. Restarting the process requires pending customers to verify again. The account session is stored for future account features; no account dashboard or purchase/points system is implemented here. Production legal text and offer conditions should be reviewed before launch.
+
+## Checks
+
+`pnpm test` exercises the request handler directly with a mocked identity verifier and in-memory SQLite, including forgery, nonce, audience, expiry, email mismatch, and duplicate-account failures. It starts no server. `pnpm build` checks JavaScript syntax; no bundler is required.
