+# The Daily Grind
+
+A static homepage using native Web Components; no bundler or framework is required. Serve the project as static files using its existing hosting setup. The existing menu, account, order, and footer URLs are retained and require routes provided by the host application.
+
+## Components
+
+`components/daily-grind.js` registers four elements, each with an open shadow root:
+
+- `<grind-navigation>`: responsive navigation with a mobile disclosure button, expanded state, and Escape handling.
+- `<grind-hero>`: the main headline, photo, and order/menu links.
+- `<coffee-card>`: a coffee article and native modal dialog. The dialog supports Escape, contained focus, an explicit close button, and focus return to its trigger.
+- `<coffee-collection>`: a slotted, responsive card grid with category filters and a polite result-count announcement. Add cards directly inside the element. Filters respond to inserted cards and changes to their category attributes.
+
+A card can be reused independently:
+
+```html
+<coffee-card
+  name="Maple Oat Latte"
+  category="seasonal"
+  label="THE SEASONAL SIP"
+  price="$5.50"
+  image="https://example.com/latte.jpg"
+  image-alt="A latte in a ceramic cup"
+  description="A short description."
+  details="The longer description shown in the dialog."
+  href="/menu/seasonal"
+  badge="Seasonal favorite"
+></coffee-card>
+```
+
+All card attributes update reactively. Categories are `seasonal` and `classics`; the default filter shows every card. `badge` is optional. Descriptive values are assigned as text; image and link URLs permit HTTP(S) and relative paths only. Components inherit `--font`, `--ink`, `--muted`, `--green`, and `--paper` design tokens. Page layout remains in `styles.css`.
+
+Photos use Unsplash; fonts use Google Fonts, with local font fallbacks. This page has no client-side dependencies or build step. JavaScript is required for the custom elements.
+
+## Checks
+
+```sh
+node --check components/daily-grind.js
+```
+
+No development server, preview server, or manual browser verification was used for this refactor.
