--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -9,6 +9,29 @@ pnpm install && pnpm run start

 The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.

+## Browser agent tools
+
+The shared layout exposes client-side [WebMCP tools](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/webmcp/imperative-api). Registration feature-detects `document.modelContext` and falls back to the earlier `navigator.modelContext` preview. Browsers without WebMCP keep the regular UI. Tools are removed and registered again during Astro navigation.
+
+| Tool | Inputs | Result |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `list_articles` | None | Article metadata and URLs |
+| `read_article` | `slug` | Article metadata and body text, without running article scripts |
+| `get_reading_list` | None | Current session's saved slugs and article metadata |
+| `open_search` | None | Opens the search form, exposing `search_articles` |
+| `open_reading_list` | None | Opens the reading-list form, exposing `update_reading_list` |
+| `search_articles` | `query` | Matching titles, summaries and URLs |
+| `update_reading_list` | `slug`, `action` (`add` or `remove`) | Updated saved slugs |
+
+The last two tools use [declarative form annotations](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/webmcp/declarative-api) and are available while their flyouts are open. They return asynchronous results through the submit event's `respondWith` method. Reading-list changes share the normal session API and update bookmark buttons. Reads and requests respect the configured base path; failed requests report errors instead of success.
+
+Run the non-browser checks with Node 24 or later:
+
+```sh
+node --test tests/browser-tools.test.mjs
+pnpm run build
+```
+
 ## Tech Stack

 - **[Astro](https://astro.build/)**: The web framework for building content-driven websites.
